  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only scvi with multiprofile is much better than PCA or scgpt, and transformer aggregation gives a small but consistent edge over avgpool (0.653 vs 0.650 accuracy). Image-only ResNet is weak, so it is unclear whether image features add complementary value to a strong RNA model. config_032 extends the best RNA setting with ResNet image and simple concat fusion, directly comparing against the RNA-only transformer baseline to isolate the effect of adding image. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the most promising RNA configuration while testing the central multimodal question with minimal added complexity."
